              ],
              "start": 0,
              "end": 92,
              "quote": "并不是所有优秀的作家都擅长拼写。如果你想让作品出版，提交一份毫无差错、呈现专业的原稿至关重要。这意味着语法正确，而且没有拼写错误。编辑大概都不会容忍一个连正确拼写单词都不肯费心的作者。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "translation:block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:2",
              "sourceParagraphIds": [
                "block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:2"
              ],
              "start": 94,
              "end": 218,
              "quote": "我的书桌上总放着两本随手可取的参考书：词典和同义词词典。我不信任笔记本电脑上的拼写检查程序。它完全不考虑语境。当然，如今网上有很多词典和同义词词典，但我还是足够老派，更喜欢有硬封面、能用手指翻页的书。我用的是《简明牛津词典》和《柯林斯同义词词典》。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "translation:block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:3",
              "sourceParagraphIds": [
                "block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:3"
              ],
              "start": 220,
              "end": 290,
              "quote": "当然，词典不仅仅是用来查拼写的。它应该给出每个词的准确定义，从而把这个词与其他意思相近却不完全相同的词区分开来。它通常还会标明这个词的发音。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "translation:block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:4",
              "sourceParagraphIds": [
                "block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:4"
              ],
              "start": 292,
              "end": 429,
              "quote": "此外，我还有一套旧的两卷本《牛津英语简编词典》，几年前在书店促销时只花了99便士买下。当然，它足有2672页，实在称不上简短。它收录了大约163000个单词，还有词语组合和惯用语。我并不经常用这部词典。不过，如果我需要查一个词的来源，或查找它的用法例句，就没有比它更好的了。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "translation:block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:5",
              "sourceParagraphIds": [
                "block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:5"
              ],
              "start": 431,
              "end": 553,
              "quote": "在长达一百多年的时间里，最有影响力的英语词典是塞缪尔·约翰逊于1755年出版的《英语词典》。约翰逊写道：“编词典是乏味的工作。”他用这句话为“乏味”的一个释义举例。不过，读词典也可以是一件乐事。花几分钟随意浏览一两页，可以是一次颇有收获的体验。"
            }
          ]
        },
        "completedSourceTexts": [
          {
            "textId": "completed:block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:1",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:1",
            "text": "Not all great writers are great spellers. If you want to be published, it’s vital to submit a perfect, professionally presented manuscript (原稿). That means good grammar and no spelling mistakes. No editor is likely to tolerate a writer who does not take the trouble to spell words correctly."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:2",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:2",
            "text": "I keep two reference books close-by on my desk: dictionary and thesaurus(同义词词典).I don’t trust my laptop’s spellchecker. It takes no account of the context. Of course, these days there are plenty of online dictionaries and thesauruses, but I’m old-fashioned enough to prefer a hard cover and pages I can leaf through with my fingers. I use the Concise Oxford Dictionary and the Collins Thesaurus."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:3",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:3",
            "text": "Of course, a dictionary is not only for spelling. It should give you a precise definition of each word, thus differentiating it from other words whose meanings are similar, but not identical. It will also usually show how the word is pronounced."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:4",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:4",
            "text": "In addition, I have an old two-volume copy of the Shorter Oxford Dictionary, picked up a few years ago in a bookshop sale for just 99 pence. Of course, with its 2,672 pages, it’s not exactly short. It contains around 163,000 words, plus word combinations and idiomatic phrases. I don’t often use this dictionary. However, if I need to check the origin of a word or to look up examples of its usage, there’s nothing better."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:5",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-gaokao-2024-i:seven-choices:5",
            "text": "For well over a hundred years the most influential English dictionary was Samuel Johnson’s Dictionary of the English Language published in 1755. \"To make dictionaries is dull (乏味) work,\" wrote Johnson, illustrating one definition of “dull”. But a dictionary can be a pleasure to read. A few minutes spent casting your eye over a page or two can be a rewarding experience."
          }
        ],
